# gitallow pattern: everything is ignored by default; only explicitly
# allowed file types/paths are tracked. Add a new `!` rule below when a
# new source file type or directory is introduced.

# 1) Ignore everything...
*
# ...but let git look inside directories to find allowed files
!*/

# 2) Allow source/config file types
!*.jl
!*.toml
!*.md
!*.yml
!*.yaml
!/docs/src/assets/documenterslate.css
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!justfile
!LICENSE

# 3) Re-ignore generated/build artifacts and local scratch state
#    (must come after the allow rules above so they take precedence)
**/Manifest.toml
/docs/build/
/docs/src/notebooks/
/docs/slate_cache/
/docs/site/
*.cov
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem
/deps/deps.jl

# 4) Never commit local agent/spec tooling (see CLAUDE.md)
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/spec.md
/specs/
/.claude/
/.specify/
